{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For there is no divination in Jacob.</b> In the language of 'I practiced divination and was blessed' (Gen. 30:27). You said: Come now with me to another place — no divination and no attempt avails against Jacob, and no sorcery avails against Israel, to curse them." "<b>As at this time it will be said of Jacob.</b> Next year, after they cross the Jordan — <b>as at this time</b> — <b>it will be said of Jacob</b>, concerning Jacob and concerning Israel, how many deeds the Holy One, blessed be He, performed for them, like 'How manifold are Your works' (Ps. 104:24), which is like 'how many are they.'" "<b>As at this time.</b> Like 'I will return to you at the time of life' (Gen. 18:10 — כעת חיה)." "<b>Of Jacob and of Israel.</b> Concerning Jacob and concerning Israel, like 'say to me, my brother' — and the reason he mentioned Jacob is because his household was complete, which was not so with Abraham and Isaac."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:30.188096558Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}